From fc107e477ec2888503f0df0b29b4c516f7c5d028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iamwrm <iamwrm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:22:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] feat(windows): opt-in TCP_NODELAY ProxyCommand relay
 for --remote

OpenSSH sets TCP_NODELAY only on interactive (tty) sessions; the remote
bridge runs 'ssh -T', so Nagle can hold a keystroke packet until the
previous one is acked - up to a full extra RTT when typing fast on a
high-latency link (i0002 W1).

New hidden subcommand 'herdr remote-tcp-relay <host> <port>' owns the TCP
connection with TCP_NODELAY set and splices it onto stdio. With
remote.tcp_relay = true (or HERDR_REMOTE_TCP_RELAY=1; requires
manage_ssh_config), the Windows launcher injects
'-o ProxyCommand="<exe>" remote-tcp-relay %h %p' next to the keepalive
flags.

Opt-in because a command-line ProxyCommand overrides any
ProxyCommand/ProxyJump from the user's ssh config for the target. Fixes
only the client->server leg; the server->client leg is sshd's socket -
measure both with HERDR_ECHO_TIMING. Unix is untouched.
